 *  the default 1.00), the terms (whole days, blank for the default 14), the late percent (two decimals, blank for the default 0.00), the policy date (yyyy-mm-dd, blank for the sheet's today), the period numbering from (yyyy-mm-dd, blank for off), terms per grade (whole days by grade, blank for the sheet's terms) and the cap (two decimals, blank for no cap) — and who makes the change, and the from-date of a dated setting by its key (yyyy-mm-dd; left out or blank for the sheet's today), and the proof threshold (two decimals, blank for none), and the note threshold (two decimals, blank for none; dated), and the permission matrix: the roles that may take each action, by action (a comma separated list of clerk and steward, blank for the standing rule), and the grace days (whole days, blank for off; not dated), and the entry date (yyyy-mm-dd, blank for off; not dated), and the grace days per grade (whole days by grade, blank for none; dated under grace-<grade>), and the proof threshold per grade (two decimals by grade, blank for the sheet's; dated under proof-threshold-<grade>), and the pot (two decimals, blank for none; not dated). */
public record SettingsRequest(String clerkLimit, String floor, String terms, String latePct, String policyDate, String periodNumberingFrom, Map<String, String> gradeTerms, String user, String cap, Map<String, String> from, String proofThreshold, Map<String, String> perms, String graceDays, String noteThreshold, String entryDate, Map<String, String> gradeGrace, Map<String, String> gradeProof, String pot) {
}
package net.officefloor.hq.app.settings;

import java.math.BigDecimal;
import java.time.LocalDate;
import java.util.Map;

/** A validated settings change on a sheet: whether the clerk limit is set and to what (null for no
 *  limit), the floor, the terms and the late percent, each null when it is not being set, and
